ldings  higher if sea sea level is rising uh  i wear the sweater because it is cold i  am adapting but that is exactly  think about what we did with the  pandemic we adapted we learned how to  wear a mask  we learned how to lock ourselves up we  learned how to not meet  friends we learned how to not hug people  we love  how that is what adaptation is and the  lesson is adaptation is  not comfortable how much harder will  that shift be will those adaptations be  especially as we're going from the end  of the pandemic  to climate change i get the feeling that  not many people are in the mood to talk  about personal sacrifice right now  but they'd rather be rewarded for a  period in which they feel like they've  already sacrificed a lot so maybe  taking more trips things like that yeah  i i think i think you're right i i in a  way i don't want to begrudge them sort  of going out  and sort of you know after having been  locked up for a year  but on the other hand this is why this  should be a moment of reflection  this should be a moment of learning  because we've also done so many things  right we  we have learned good lessons we have  learned the lesson that if you spend a  dollar  in advance to avert a crisis  you will save millions of dollars when  if the crisis hits  so i think those are the lessons that  come now in terms of climate and  pandemic in particular  in the beginning there was a little sort  of thought that okay we won't be driving  as much and we won't be  using energy as much and the consumption  will go down  i'm not sure that has exactly happened  maybe it's happened in a few cases  to the extent it has happened you know  climate strategy should not be locking  people up in their homes  and on the other hand we have found that  you know we are a consumptive species we  find new ways to consume  we pay other people to come and and  travel on our behalf and emit carbon on  our behalf and develop  and and drop food at our doorsteps but  we  are a we ar